      "created_at": "2016-11-11T20:50:15Z",
      "updated_at": "2016-11-11T20:53:33Z",
      "body": "Isomorphic React isn't a framework. It just means writing your code so it runs both on the client and the server. The server obviously doesn't have things like localStorage/sessionStorage/cookies, at least not out of the box (there are many polyfills for Node to fill in some of this functionality, but they vary widely in quality and how recenlty they've been updated). So writing your library in such a way that it assumes those things exist means your library just can't be easily used isomorphically.\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
